│ intestine", "abstract": "The use of the anti-inflammatory drug indomethacin (INDO) in preterm infants has been       │
│ associated with an increased risk of developing enteropathies. In this study, we have investigated the direct impact │
│ of INDO on the human mid-gestation intestinal transcriptome using serum-free organ culture. After determining the    │
│ optimal dose of 1 μM of INDO (90% inhibition of intestinal prostaglandin E2 production and range of circulating      │
│ levels in treated preterm babies), global gene expression profiles were determined using Illumina bead chip          │
│ microarrays in both small and large intestines after 48 h of INDO treatment. Using Ingenuity Pathway Analysis        │
